<title>PHILIPPINES: WG&amp;A collects insurance on sunken ship.</title>
<headline>WG&amp;A collects insurance on sunken ship.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shipping firm WG&amp;A said on Tuesday it has collected the full insurance of 410 million pesos for its luxury ship that caught fire and sank late last month.</p>
<p>&quot;We are happy to advise that the full insurance amount of 410 million pesos has been fully paid by our insurer, the Insular General Insurance Co Inc.,&quot; corporate secretary Eugene Espedido said in a statement.</p>
<p>Espedido said the &quot;carrying value&quot; of its MV Super Ferry 7 was 448 million pesos.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
